SCIF loader for the IMDT V2H and V2N SBCs
=========================================

A replacement for Renesas Flash Writer. It brings the board up to a fastboot
U-Boot from a serial cable alone, with nothing written to flash, and fastboot
then writes BL2, the FIP or the eMMC.

Build
-----

    tools/imdt/v2h-build-loader.sh v2h-fastboot.img
    tools/imdt/v2n-build-loader.sh v2n-fastboot.img

This builds the SPL (imdt-v2h-sbc-spl_defconfig) and the fastboot-only U-Boot
(imdt-v2h-sbc-fastboot_defconfig) and bundles them with the DDR PHY firmware.
The V2N uses the imdt-v2n-sbc-* defconfigs. Its code is under
board/imdt/imdt-v2n-sbc/tfa and it shares spl.c and glue.c with the V2H. The
PHY firmware is identical, so both boards use the same blob.

Boot flow
---------

1. Boot mode "prog" (SCIF download). The boot ROM takes the SPL as an srec
   over SCIF at 115200 baud into SRAM. The ROM refuses an image over 224 KiB.
2. The SPL releases SCIF0 from reset and module stop, runs the TF-A CPG, PFC
   and TZC setup (copied under tfa/) and switches SCIF to 921600 baud.
3. The host sends the DDR PHY firmware into SRAM. The SPL trains DRAM.
4. The host sends the second stage into DRAM at 0x50000000 and the SPL jumps
   to it. That is the fastboot-only U-Boot, running at EL3 without BL31, so it
   is for flashing and not for booting Linux.

Each transfer is "FBLD", u32 address, u32 length, payload, u32 byte sum.
Booting to fastboot takes about 19 seconds.

ROM image
---------

The ROM wants a 512 byte header at 0x08101E00 (size, 0x200, load address
0x08108000, 0x55 0xaa at the end) and the body at 0x08108000. It rejects S5
records. tools/imdt/v2h-spl-srec.sh adds the header.

Flashing
--------

    fastboot stage fip.bin
    fastboot oem run:"sf probe; sf erase 0x60000 0x120000; sf write 0x62000000 0x60000 0x120000"

BL2 lives at 0x0 and the FIP at 0x60000. eMMC images go through "fastboot
flash". Console output of "oem run" appears on the serial console only.
